[The term] "land subdivision" includes all divisions of a tract or parcel of land into two or more lots, building sites, or other division for the purpose, whether immediate or future, of sale, legacy, or building development, and includes all division of land involving a new street or a change in existing streets, and includes resubdivision and, where appropriate to the context, relates to the process of subdividing or to the land or area subdivided; provided, however, that the following are not included within this definition:
A. The combination of previously platted lots or the division of an existing lot between adjoining lots which are unaltered from the approved plat, where the total number of lots is reduced and the resultant lots are equal to the standards set forth in this title;
B. The division of land into parcels of five acres or more where no new street is involved, provided lot depth does not exceed twice the width at the building line;
C. The division of land in nonresidential zoning districts where no minimum lot size is specified and no new street is involved, provided lot depth does not exceed twice the width of the building line;
D. A filing fee to cover the cost of investigation and review of the subdivision; the cost of filing the plat; and the cost of reproducing the necessary copies shall be charged to the subdivider according to the schedule posted in City Hall.
(Prior Code, § 16.04.020; Ord. No. 694, 4-27-1998; Ord. No. 668, § SR1-2, 5-13-1996)

1110:
A. Scale. The preliminary plat shall be clearly and legibly drawn at a scale of not more than one hundred (100) feet to one inch.
B. Sheet Size. Sheet size shall be eighteen (18) inches by twenty-four (24) inches. If the complete plat cannot be shown on one sheet of this size, it may be shown on more than one sheet with an index map on a separate sheet of the same size.
C. Ground Elevations. The preliminary plat shall show ground elevations by contours at intervals of not more than two feet, based on a datum plane approved by the building department of the city. If any part of the land platted lies within a flood hazard district, as defined by the zoning ordinance of the city, elevations shall be referenced to the National Geodetic Vertical Datum of 1929 and the boundaries of that district shall be drawn on the plat.
Ground elevation contours shall not be required for minor subdivisions, provided that: (1) no part of the land lies within a flood hazard district; and (2) the lots are small enough or the topography so little varied that suitability of the lots as building sites can be determined readily by visual inspection.
D. Information to be Provided on Preliminary Plat. The preliminary plat shall contain the following information:
1. Name and address of owner of record and of subdivider;
2. Proposed name of subdivision;
3. North point, graphic scale and date;
4. Vicinity map showing location and acreage of the subdivision;
5. Exact boundary lines of the tract by lengths and bearings;
6. Names of owners of record of adjoining land;
7. Existing streets and utilities on and adjacent to the tract;
8. Proposed layout, including streets and alleys with proposed street names, right-of-way and pavement widths, lot lines with approximate dimensions, easements, land to be reserved or dedicated for public uses, and any land to be used for purposes other than single-family dwellings;
9. Locations of existing and proposed water supply, sanitary sewerage, and storm drainage lines and structures;
10. Such street cross-sections and centerline profiles as may be required by the secretary of the planning commission.
E. Certificate of Tentative Approval. A certificate of tentative approval of the preliminary plat by the planning commission shall be inscribed on the plat as follows:
Pursuant to the Land Subdivision Regulations of the City of Grantville, Georgia, all the requirements of tentative approval having been fulfilled, this preliminary plat was given tentative approval by the Planning Commission at its meeting on ________, 20___.
_____ Date | _____ Secretary, Planning Commission
(Prior Code, § 16.08.040; Ord. No. 668, § SR 2-4, 5-13-1996)
